            <ArticleTitle>Training in paediatric cardiac surgery: the history and role of training in a different country and even overseas.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1491-1493</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1017/S1047951116001700</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper presents a personal perspective on the value of training overseas in paediatric cardiac surgery. From personal experience and observation, I argue that travel does indeed broaden the mind and placing artificial constraints on movement of trainees is a negative move. We need to work with others, in other cultures to become rounded human beings. And to be an empathetic surgeon, you need to be a rounded human being.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
